{"id":"ea3339e0eaafb915","time":1795635727,"message":"Rename parallel.taken to map_worker","changes":[{"name":"parallel.map","kind":"fn","old":"443ffbf513f76a73","new":"05e9f4174f2c8596","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"parallel","text":"/// The same list as `xs.map(f)`, computed on `workers()` threads. Each\n/// worker takes the next index from a shared counter, so a slow element\n/// doesn't hold up the ones after it.\n/// \n/// Objects made before the workers start are pinned while they run\n/// (`driver_keep_shared`). Objects the workers make are counted as usual.\n/// `f` may only read shared data: no timings, no files.\npub fn map[T, R](xs: List[T], f: (T) -> R) -> List[R] {\n  n := min(parallel.workers(), len(xs))\n  if n <= 1 {\n    return xs.map(f)\n  }\n  match parallel.driver_keep_shared(1).to_int() {\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  c := parallel.work_counter()\n  parts := scope {\n    mut hs := []\n    for _ in 0..n {\n      mut hs.push(spawn parallel.map_worker(xs, f, c))\n    }\n    await hs\n  }\n  match parallel.driver_keep_shared(0).to_int() {\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  mut at := Dict[Int, R] {}\n  for part in parts {\n    for (i, r) in part {\n      mut at.insert(i, r)\n    }\n  }\n  mut out := []\n  for i in 0..len(xs) {\n    match get(at, i) {\n      Some(r) => mut out.push(r),\n      None => (),\n    }\n  }\n  out\n}","old_text":"/// The same list as `xs.map(f)`, computed on `workers()` threads. Each\n/// worker takes the next index from a shared counter, so a slow element\n/// doesn't hold up the ones after it.\n/// \n/// Objects made before the workers start are pinned while they run\n/// (`driver_keep_shared`). Objects the workers make are counted as usual.\n/// `f` may only read shared data: no timings, no files.\npub fn map[T, R](xs: List[T], f: (T) -> R) -> List[R] {\n  n := min(parallel.workers(), len(xs))\n  if n <= 1 {\n    return xs.map(f)\n  }\n  match parallel.driver_keep_shared(1).to_int() {\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  c := parallel.work_counter()\n  parts := scope {\n    mut hs := []\n    for _ in 0..n {\n      mut hs.push(spawn parallel.taken(xs, f, c))\n    }\n    await hs\n  }\n  match parallel.driver_keep_shared(0).to_int() {\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  mut at := Dict[Int, R] {}\n  for part in parts {\n    for (i, r) in part {\n      mut at.insert(i, r)\n    }\n  }\n  mut out := []\n  for i in 0..len(xs) {\n    match get(at, i) {\n      Some(r) => mut out.push(r),\n      None => (),\n    }\n  }\n  out\n}"},{"name":"parallel.map_worker","kind":"fn","old":null,"new":"63f4ef2130433360","interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"parallel","text":"/// One worker of `map`: takes indices from `c` until past the end, and\n/// returns each result with its index.\nfn map_worker[T, R](xs: List[T], f: (T) -> R, c: I64) -> List[(Int, R)] {\n  mut out := []\n  while true {\n    i := parallel.work_take(c).to_int()\n    match get(xs, i) {\n      Some(x) => mut out.push((i, f(x))),\n      None => return out,\n    }\n  }\n  out\n}"},{"name":"parallel.taken","kind":"fn","old":"0bb92c4b4d19f3ec","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"parallel","old_text":"/// One worker of `map`: takes indices from `c` until past the end, and\n/// returns each result with its index.\nfn taken[T, R](xs: List[T], f: (T) -> R, c: I64) -> List[(Int, R)] {\n  mut out := []\n  while true {\n    i := parallel.work_take(c).to_int()\n    match get(xs, i) {\n      Some(x) => mut out.push((i, f(x))),\n      None => return out,\n    }\n  }\n  out\n}"}],"renames":[{"from":"parallel.taken","to":"parallel.map_worker","kind":"function"}],"references":["parallel.map"]}
{"id":"600bc14a30cd423d","time":1795633863,"message":"rename parse.rust_quoted → parse.debug_quoted","changes":[{"name":"parse.debug_quoted","kind":"fn","old":null,"new":"d0100485f6af55d1","interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"parse","text":"/// A string as Rust's `{:?}` writes it.\nfn debug_quoted(s: String) -> String {\n  \"\\\"\"\n    + replace(replace(replace(\n      replace(replace(s, \"\\\\\", \"\\\\\\\\\"), \"\\\"\", \"\\\\\\\"\"),\n      \"\\n\",\n      \"\\\\n\",\n    ), \"\\t\", \"\\\\t\"), \"\\r\", \"\\r\")\n    + \"\\\"\"\n}"},{"name":"parse.tok_shown","kind":"fn","old":"5eb40b9488e39591","new":"0e4a3ee5193232bc","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"parse","text":"/// A token as it is written, in messages: `` `)` ``, `` `pub` ``, `` `3` ``,\n/// a string as its literal; the end of the text.\nfn tok_shown(t: lex.Tok) -> String {\n  match t {\n    lex.IntTok(v) => \"`\" + to_string(v) + \"`\",\n    lex.BigIntTok(s) => \"`\" + s + \"`\",\n    lex.FloatTok(f) => \"`\" + to_string(f) + \"`\",\n    lex.StrTok(s) => \"`\" + parse.debug_quoted(s) + \"`\",\n    lex.FStrTok(_) => \"an f-string\",\n    lex.Ident(s) => \"`\" + s + \"`\",\n    lex.HoleTok(s) => \"`?\" + s + \"`\",\n    lex.DocTok(_) => \"a doc comment (`///`)\",\n    lex.Sym(s) => \"`\" + s + \"`\",\n    lex.Eof => \"the end\",\n  }\n}","old_text":"/// A token as it is written, in messages: `` `)` ``, `` `pub` ``, `` `3` ``,\n/// a string as its literal; the end of the text.\nfn tok_shown(t: lex.Tok) -> String {\n  match t {\n    lex.IntTok(v) => \"`\" + to_string(v) + \"`\",\n    lex.BigIntTok(s) => \"`\" + s + \"`\",\n    lex.FloatTok(f) => \"`\" + to_string(f) + \"`\",\n    lex.StrTok(s) => \"`\" + parse.rust_quoted(s) + \"`\",\n    lex.FStrTok(_) => \"an f-string\",\n    lex.Ident(s) => \"`\" + s + \"`\",\n    lex.HoleTok(s) => \"`?\" + s + \"`\",\n    lex.DocTok(_) => \"a doc comment (`///`)\",\n    lex.Sym(s) => \"`\" + s + \"`\",\n    lex.Eof => \"the end\",\n  }\n}"},{"name":"parse.rust_quoted","kind":"fn","old":"d2b5ee275429cfb3","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"parse","old_text":"/// A string as Rust's `{:?}` writes it.\nfn rust_quoted(s: String) -> String {\n  \"\\\"\"\n    + replace(replace(replace(\n      replace(replace(s, \"\\\\\", \"\\\\\\\\\"), \"\\\"\", \"\\\\\\\"\"),\n      \"\\n\",\n      \"\\\\n\",\n    ), \"\\t\", \"\\\\t\"), \"\\r\", \"\\r\")\n    + \"\\\"\"\n}"}],"renames":[{"from":"parse.rust_quoted","to":"parse.debug_quoted","kind":"function"}],"references":["parse.tok_shown"]}
{"id":"fbc4f0684f354c83","time":1795634364,"message":"rename desugar.sweet → desugar.unsugared","changes":[{"name":"desugar.unsugared","kind":"fn","old":null,"new":"13e681b3f3434961","interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"desugar","text":"/// `e` without sugar, innermost first (so what is rebuilt holds none).\nfn unsugared(e: ast.Expr) -> ast.Expr {\n  match e {\n    // a slice's range stays a range until the slice is rewritten\n    ast.Index { base, index: ast.Range { lo, hi, inclusive } } => desugar.sliced(desugar.unsugared(base), match lo {\n      Some(x) => desugar.unsugared(x),\n      None => ast.IntLit(0),\n    }, match hi {\n      Some(x) => Some(desugar.unsugared(x)),\n      None => None,\n    }, inclusive),\n    // an element assigned (`xs[i] = v`): the list's place assigned a new\n    // list, before the rest is rewritten\n    ast.Block { stmts, last } => if stmts.any(s -> desugar.element_assign(s)) {\n      desugar.unsugared(ast.Block {\n        stmts: stmts.map(s -> desugar.elements_assigned(s)),\n        last,\n      })\n    } else {\n      desugar.sugar(walk.expr_children(\n        e,\n        x -> desugar.unsugared(x),\n        t -> desugar.sweet_type(t),\n      ))\n    },\n    _ => desugar.sugar(walk.expr_children(\n      e,\n      x -> desugar.unsugared(x),\n      t -> desugar.sweet_type(t),\n    )),\n  }\n}"},{"name":"desugar.sweet_type","kind":"fn","old":"d7a335684d7cc157","new":"700d58d2046ab9ff","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"desugar","text":"fn sweet_type(t: ast.TypeExpr) -> ast.TypeExpr {\n  walk.type_children(\n    t,\n    x -> desugar.unsugared(x),\n    u -> desugar.sweet_type(u),\n  )\n}","old_text":"fn sweet_type(t: ast.TypeExpr) -> ast.TypeExpr {\n  walk.type_children(\n    t,\n    x -> desugar.sweet(x),\n    u -> desugar.sweet_type(u),\n  )\n}"},{"name":"desugar.desugar_more","kind":"fn","old":"ed8b834873a21e06","new":"753a829d82bf4136","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"desugar","text":"/// `desugar` of definitions added to a program already without its sugar\n/// (`context`, not returned), each definition of the program desugared once:\n/// `new` without sugar, with the aliases made for refinements no definition\n/// of the program had yet; the errors; and the refinements given an alias so\n/// far (`texts`, then the new ones: `$where_k` is the `k`th).\npub fn desugar_more(\n  new: List[ast.Decl],\n  context: List[ast.Decl],\n  texts: List[String],\n) -> (List[ast.Decl], List[(String, String)], List[String]) {\n  mut errors := []\n  mut out := []\n  for d0 in desugar.with_models(new, context) {\n    // (an `extern python` function: the call of the Python worker)\n    d := desugar.python_lowered(d0)\n    for e in walk.decl_kids(d).1 {\n      for _ in 0..desugar.open_ranges(e) {\n        mut errors.push(\n          (\n            desugar.decl_name(d),\n            \"a range needs both ends (`a..b`), except in a slice: `xs[a..]`, `xs[..b]`\",\n          ),\n        )\n      }\n    }\n    mut out.push(\n      desugar.named_results(walk.decl_parts(\n        d,\n        x -> desugar.unsugared(x),\n        t -> desugar.sweet_type(t),\n      )),\n    )\n  }\n  (refined, all) := desugar.inline_refinements(\n    desugar.key_paths(desugar.defaults(out, context), context),\n    texts,\n  )\n  (desugar.mixed_unions(refined), errors, all)\n}","old_text":"/// `desugar` of definitions added to a program already without its sugar\n/// (`context`, not returned), each definition of the program desugared once:\n/// `new` without sugar, with the aliases made for refinements no definition\n/// of the program had yet; the errors; and the refinements given an alias so\n/// far (`texts`, then the new ones: `$where_k` is the `k`th).\npub fn desugar_more(\n  new: List[ast.Decl],\n  context: List[ast.Decl],\n  texts: List[String],\n) -> (List[ast.Decl], List[(String, String)], List[String]) {\n  mut errors := []\n  mut out := []\n  for d0 in desugar.with_models(new, context) {\n    // (an `extern python` function: the call of the Python worker)\n    d := desugar.python_lowered(d0)\n    for e in walk.decl_kids(d).1 {\n      for _ in 0..desugar.open_ranges(e) {\n        mut errors.push(\n          (\n            desugar.decl_name(d),\n            \"a range needs both ends (`a..b`), except in a slice: `xs[a..]`, `xs[..b]`\",\n          ),\n        )\n      }\n    }\n    mut out.push(\n      desugar.named_results(walk.decl_parts(\n        d,\n        x -> desugar.sweet(x),\n        t -> desugar.sweet_type(t),\n      )),\n    )\n  }\n  (refined, all) := desugar.inline_refinements(\n    desugar.key_paths(desugar.defaults(out, context), context),\n    texts,\n  )\n  (desugar.mixed_unions(refined), errors, all)\n}"},{"name":"desugar.sweet","kind":"fn","old":"1d8ec2a78c57786b","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"desugar","old_text":"/// `e` without sugar, innermost first (so what is rebuilt holds none).\nfn sweet(e: ast.Expr) -> ast.Expr {\n  match e {\n    // a slice's range stays a range until the slice is rewritten\n    ast.Index { base, index: ast.Range { lo, hi, inclusive } } => desugar.sliced(desugar.sweet(base), match lo {\n      Some(x) => desugar.sweet(x),\n      None => ast.IntLit(0),\n    }, match hi {\n      Some(x) => Some(desugar.sweet(x)),\n      None => None,\n    }, inclusive),\n    // an element assigned (`xs[i] = v`): the list's place assigned a new\n    // list, before the rest is rewritten\n    ast.Block { stmts, last } => if stmts.any(s -> desugar.element_assign(s)) {\n      desugar.sweet(ast.Block {\n        stmts: stmts.map(s -> desugar.elements_assigned(s)),\n        last,\n      })\n    } else {\n      desugar.sugar(walk.expr_children(\n        e,\n        x -> desugar.sweet(x),\n        t -> desugar.sweet_type(t),\n      ))\n    },\n    _ => desugar.sugar(walk.expr_children(\n      e,\n      x -> desugar.sweet(x),\n      t -> desugar.sweet_type(t),\n    )),\n  }\n}"}],"renames":[{"from":"desugar.sweet","to":"desugar.unsugared","kind":"function"}],"references":["desugar.sweet_type","desugar.desugar_more"]}
{"id":"7273da6eb38ee6fd","time":1795634366,"message":"rename desugar.sugar → desugar.unsugared_node","changes":[{"name":"desugar.unsugared","kind":"fn","old":"13e681b3f3434961","new":"d023c3becab1943b","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"desugar","text":"/// `e` without sugar, innermost first (so what is rebuilt holds none).\nfn unsugared(e: ast.Expr) -> ast.Expr {\n  match e {\n    // a slice's range stays a range until the slice is rewritten\n    ast.Index { base, index: ast.Range { lo, hi, inclusive } } => desugar.sliced(desugar.unsugared(base), match lo {\n      Some(x) => desugar.unsugared(x),\n      None => ast.IntLit(0),\n    }, match hi {\n      Some(x) => Some(desugar.unsugared(x)),\n      None => None,\n    }, inclusive),\n    // an element assigned (`xs[i] = v`): the list's place assigned a new\n    // list, before the rest is rewritten\n    ast.Block { stmts, last } => if stmts.any(s -> desugar.element_assign(s)) {\n      desugar.unsugared(ast.Block {\n        stmts: stmts.map(s -> desugar.elements_assigned(s)),\n        last,\n      })\n    } else {\n      desugar.unsugared_node(walk.expr_children(\n        e,\n        x -> desugar.unsugared(x),\n        t -> desugar.sweet_type(t),\n      ))\n    },\n    _ => desugar.unsugared_node(walk.expr_children(\n      e,\n      x -> desugar.unsugared(x),\n      t -> desugar.sweet_type(t),\n    )),\n  }\n}","old_text":"/// `e` without sugar, innermost first (so what is rebuilt holds none).\nfn unsugared(e: ast.Expr) -> ast.Expr {\n  match e {\n    // a slice's range stays a range until the slice is rewritten\n    ast.Index { base, index: ast.Range { lo, hi, inclusive } } => desugar.sliced(desugar.unsugared(base), match lo {\n      Some(x) => desugar.unsugared(x),\n      None => ast.IntLit(0),\n    }, match hi {\n      Some(x) => Some(desugar.unsugared(x)),\n      None => None,\n    }, inclusive),\n    // an element assigned (`xs[i] = v`): the list's place assigned a new\n    // list, before the rest is rewritten\n    ast.Block { stmts, last } => if stmts.any(s -> desugar.element_assign(s)) {\n      desugar.unsugared(ast.Block {\n        stmts: stmts.map(s -> desugar.elements_assigned(s)),\n        last,\n      })\n    } else {\n      desugar.sugar(walk.expr_children(\n        e,\n        x -> desugar.unsugared(x),\n        t -> desugar.sweet_type(t),\n      ))\n    },\n    _ => desugar.sugar(walk.expr_children(\n      e,\n      x -> desugar.unsugared(x),\n      t -> desugar.sweet_type(t),\n    )),\n  }\n}"},{"name":"desugar.unsugared_node","kind":"fn","old":null,"new":"eea2c5ccebbde9b4","interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"desugar","text":"/// One node rewritten, its children already without sugar.\nfn unsugared_node(e: ast.Expr) -> ast.Expr {\n  match e {\n    ast.Range { lo: Some(lo), hi: Some(hi), inclusive } => desugar.call(\"range\", [lo, if inclusive {\n      desugar.plus_one(hi)\n    } else {\n      hi\n    }]),\n    // (reported by `open_ranges`)\n    ast.Range { .. } => ast.UnitExpr,\n    ast.Index { base, index } => desugar.call(\"at\", [base, index]),\n    ast.Comp { kind, elem, fors } => {\n      list := desugar.comprehension(elem, fors)\n      match kind {\n        ast.ListComp => list,\n        ast.SetComp => desugar.call(\"set\", [list]),\n        ast.DictComp => desugar.call(\"dict\", [list]),\n      }\n    },\n    ast.DictExpr { types, entries } => desugar.typed(\"Dict\", types, desugar.call(\n      \"dict\",\n      [ast.ListExpr(entries.map(kv -> ast.TupleExpr([kv.0, kv.1])))],\n    )),\n    ast.SetExpr { types, elems } => desugar.typed(\n      \"Set\",\n      types,\n      desugar.call(\"set\", [ast.ListExpr(elems)]),\n    ),\n    _ => e,\n  }\n}"},{"name":"desugar.sugar","kind":"fn","old":"1db356f0b906a203","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"desugar","old_text":"/// One node rewritten, its children already without sugar.\nfn sugar(e: ast.Expr) -> ast.Expr {\n  match e {\n    ast.Range { lo: Some(lo), hi: Some(hi), inclusive } => desugar.call(\"range\", [lo, if inclusive {\n      desugar.plus_one(hi)\n    } else {\n      hi\n    }]),\n    // (reported by `open_ranges`)\n    ast.Range { .. } => ast.UnitExpr,\n    ast.Index { base, index } => desugar.call(\"at\", [base, index]),\n    ast.Comp { kind, elem, fors } => {\n      list := desugar.comprehension(elem, fors)\n      match kind {\n        ast.ListComp => list,\n        ast.SetComp => desugar.call(\"set\", [list]),\n        ast.DictComp => desugar.call(\"dict\", [list]),\n      }\n    },\n    ast.DictExpr { types, entries } => desugar.typed(\"Dict\", types, desugar.call(\n      \"dict\",\n      [ast.ListExpr(entries.map(kv -> ast.TupleExpr([kv.0, kv.1])))],\n    )),\n    ast.SetExpr { types, elems } => desugar.typed(\n      \"Set\",\n      types,\n      desugar.call(\"set\", [ast.ListExpr(elems)]),\n    ),\n    _ => e,\n  }\n}"}],"renames":[{"from":"desugar.sugar","to":"desugar.unsugared_node","kind":"function"}],"references":["desugar.unsugared"]}
{"id":"044c102c4f6e87a8","time":1795634369,"message":"rename desugar.sweet_type → desugar.unsugared_type","changes":[{"name":"desugar.unsugared","kind":"fn","old":"d023c3becab1943b","new":"ecc09e0f989648ce","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"desugar","text":"/// `e` without sugar, innermost first (so what is rebuilt holds none).\nfn unsugared(e: ast.Expr) -> ast.Expr {\n  match e {\n    // a slice's range stays a range until the slice is rewritten\n    ast.Index { base, index: ast.Range { lo, hi, inclusive } } => desugar.sliced(desugar.unsugared(base), match lo {\n      Some(x) => desugar.unsugared(x),\n      None => ast.IntLit(0),\n    }, match hi {\n      Some(x) => Some(desugar.unsugared(x)),\n      None => None,\n    }, inclusive),\n    // an element assigned (`xs[i] = v`): the list's place assigned a new\n    // list, before the rest is rewritten\n    ast.Block { stmts, last } => if stmts.any(s -> desugar.element_assign(s)) {\n      desugar.unsugared(ast.Block {\n        stmts: stmts.map(s -> desugar.elements_assigned(s)),\n        last,\n      })\n    } else {\n      desugar.unsugared_node(walk.expr_children(\n        e,\n        x -> desugar.unsugared(x),\n        t -> desugar.unsugared_type(t),\n      ))\n    },\n    _ => desugar.unsugared_node(walk.expr_children(\n      e,\n      x -> desugar.unsugared(x),\n      t -> desugar.unsugared_type(t),\n    )),\n  }\n}","old_text":"/// `e` without sugar, innermost first (so what is rebuilt holds none).\nfn unsugared(e: ast.Expr) -> ast.Expr {\n  match e {\n    // a slice's range stays a range until the slice is rewritten\n    ast.Index { base, index: ast.Range { lo, hi, inclusive } } => desugar.sliced(desugar.unsugared(base), match lo {\n      Some(x) => desugar.unsugared(x),\n      None => ast.IntLit(0),\n    }, match hi {\n      Some(x) => Some(desugar.unsugared(x)),\n      None => None,\n    }, inclusive),\n    // an element assigned (`xs[i] = v`): the list's place assigned a new\n    // list, before the rest is rewritten\n    ast.Block { stmts, last } => if stmts.any(s -> desugar.element_assign(s)) {\n      desugar.unsugared(ast.Block {\n        stmts: stmts.map(s -> desugar.elements_assigned(s)),\n        last,\n      })\n    } else {\n      desugar.unsugared_node(walk.expr_children(\n        e,\n        x -> desugar.unsugared(x),\n        t -> desugar.sweet_type(t),\n      ))\n    },\n    _ => desugar.unsugared_node(walk.expr_children(\n      e,\n      x -> desugar.unsugared(x),\n      t -> desugar.sweet_type(t),\n    )),\n  }\n}"},{"name":"desugar.unsugared_type","kind":"fn","old":null,"new":"4124a06963a424ff","interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"desugar","text":"fn unsugared_type(t: ast.TypeExpr) -> ast.TypeExpr {\n  walk.type_children(\n    t,\n    x -> desugar.unsugared(x),\n    u -> desugar.unsugared_type(u),\n  )\n}"},{"name":"desugar.desugar_more","kind":"fn","old":"753a829d82bf4136","new":"2e35a7d812d28aaf","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"desugar","text":"/// `desugar` of definitions added to a program already without its sugar\n/// (`context`, not returned), each definition of the program desugared once:\n/// `new` without sugar, with the aliases made for refinements no definition\n/// of the program had yet; the errors; and the refinements given an alias so\n/// far (`texts`, then the new ones: `$where_k` is the `k`th).\npub fn desugar_more(\n  new: List[ast.Decl],\n  context: List[ast.Decl],\n  texts: List[String],\n) -> (List[ast.Decl], List[(String, String)], List[String]) {\n  mut errors := []\n  mut out := []\n  for d0 in desugar.with_models(new, context) {\n    // (an `extern python` function: the call of the Python worker)\n    d := desugar.python_lowered(d0)\n    for e in walk.decl_kids(d).1 {\n      for _ in 0..desugar.open_ranges(e) {\n        mut errors.push(\n          (\n            desugar.decl_name(d),\n            \"a range needs both ends (`a..b`), except in a slice: `xs[a..]`, `xs[..b]`\",\n          ),\n        )\n      }\n    }\n    mut out.push(\n      desugar.named_results(walk.decl_parts(\n        d,\n        x -> desugar.unsugared(x),\n        t -> desugar.unsugared_type(t),\n      )),\n    )\n  }\n  (refined, all) := desugar.inline_refinements(\n    desugar.key_paths(desugar.defaults(out, context), context),\n    texts,\n  )\n  (desugar.mixed_unions(refined), errors, all)\n}","old_text":"/// `desugar` of definitions added to a program already without its sugar\n/// (`context`, not returned), each definition of the program desugared once:\n/// `new` without sugar, with the aliases made for refinements no definition\n/// of the program had yet; the errors; and the refinements given an alias so\n/// far (`texts`, then the new ones: `$where_k` is the `k`th).\npub fn desugar_more(\n  new: List[ast.Decl],\n  context: List[ast.Decl],\n  texts: List[String],\n) -> (List[ast.Decl], List[(String, String)], List[String]) {\n  mut errors := []\n  mut out := []\n  for d0 in desugar.with_models(new, context) {\n    // (an `extern python` function: the call of the Python worker)\n    d := desugar.python_lowered(d0)\n    for e in walk.decl_kids(d).1 {\n      for _ in 0..desugar.open_ranges(e) {\n        mut errors.push(\n          (\n            desugar.decl_name(d),\n            \"a range needs both ends (`a..b`), except in a slice: `xs[a..]`, `xs[..b]`\",\n          ),\n        )\n      }\n    }\n    mut out.push(\n      desugar.named_results(walk.decl_parts(\n        d,\n        x -> desugar.unsugared(x),\n        t -> desugar.sweet_type(t),\n      )),\n    )\n  }\n  (refined, all) := desugar.inline_refinements(\n    desugar.key_paths(desugar.defaults(out, context), context),\n    texts,\n  )\n  (desugar.mixed_unions(refined), errors, all)\n}"},{"name":"desugar.sweet_type","kind":"fn","old":"700d58d2046ab9ff","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"desugar","old_text":"fn sweet_type(t: ast.TypeExpr) -> ast.TypeExpr {\n  walk.type_children(\n    t,\n    x -> desugar.unsugared(x),\n    u -> desugar.sweet_type(u),\n  )\n}"}],"renames":[{"from":"desugar.sweet_type","to":"desugar.unsugared_type","kind":"function"}],"references":["desugar.unsugared","desugar.desugar_more"]}
{"id":"52afca44b1896d90","time":1795635050,"message":"rename lint.old_forms → lint.functional_forms","changes":[{"name":"lint.collection_forms","kind":"fn","old":"1a227912651478d9","new":"a4db1fa0f8aa2163","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"lint","text":"/// Lists, dicts and sets change through `mut` methods, and new ones come\n/// from expressions.\n/// - Changing: `xs = push(xs, x)` is `mut xs.push(x)`,\n/// `d = insert(d, k, v)` is `mut d.insert(k, v)`, `xs = sort(xs)` is\n/// `mut xs.sort()`.\n/// - New values: `xs + [x]` for `push(xs, x)`, `xs.sorted()` for\n/// `sort(xs)`, `xs.sorted_by(f)`, `xs.reversed()` for `reverse(xs)` (of a\n/// string too), and a changed copy for a dict or set with one entry more\n/// or less (`{ mut copy := d; mut copy.insert(k, v); copy }`).\n/// Syntactic: a program function named `push` (`insert`, ...) is rewritten\n/// too, and a method of that name only where its result is assigned back\n/// to its receiver.\nfn collection_forms(d: ast.Decl) -> (List[String], ast.Decl) {\n  changed := walk.decl_parts(\n    d,\n    e -> lint.collections_fixed(e),\n    t -> walk.rewrite_type(t, e -> lint.collections_fixed(e)),\n  )\n  if changed == d {\n    return ([], d)\n  }\n  found := walk.decl_exprs(d)\n    .map(e -> lint.functional_forms(e))\n    .fold([], (a, b) -> a + b)\n  mut names: List[String] = []\n  for n in found {\n    if !names.contains(n) {\n      names += [n]\n    }\n  }\n  shown := names.map(n -> \"`\" + n + \"`\").join(\", \")\n  w := f\"`{lint.shown_name(d)}`: {shown} as functions: a list, dict or set changes by a `mut` method (`mut xs.push(x)`), a new one is an expression (`xs + [x]`, `xs.sorted()`)\"\n  ([w], changed)\n}","old_text":"/// Lists, dicts and sets change through `mut` methods, and new ones come\n/// from expressions.\n/// - Changing: `xs = push(xs, x)` is `mut xs.push(x)`,\n/// `d = insert(d, k, v)` is `mut d.insert(k, v)`, `xs = sort(xs)` is\n/// `mut xs.sort()`.\n/// - New values: `xs + [x]` for `push(xs, x)`, `xs.sorted()` for\n/// `sort(xs)`, `xs.sorted_by(f)`, `xs.reversed()` for `reverse(xs)` (of a\n/// string too), and a changed copy for a dict or set with one entry more\n/// or less (`{ mut copy := d; mut copy.insert(k, v); copy }`).\n/// Syntactic: a program function named `push` (`insert`, ...) is rewritten\n/// too, and a method of that name only where its result is assigned back\n/// to its receiver.\nfn collection_forms(d: ast.Decl) -> (List[String], ast.Decl) {\n  changed := walk.decl_parts(\n    d,\n    e -> lint.collections_fixed(e),\n    t -> walk.rewrite_type(t, e -> lint.collections_fixed(e)),\n  )\n  if changed == d {\n    return ([], d)\n  }\n  found := walk.decl_exprs(d)\n    .map(e -> lint.old_forms(e))\n    .fold([], (a, b) -> a + b)\n  mut names: List[String] = []\n  for n in found {\n    if !names.contains(n) {\n      names += [n]\n    }\n  }\n  shown := names.map(n -> \"`\" + n + \"`\").join(\", \")\n  w := f\"`{lint.shown_name(d)}`: {shown} as functions: a list, dict or set changes by a `mut` method (`mut xs.push(x)`), a new one is an expression (`xs + [x]`, `xs.sorted()`)\"\n  ([w], changed)\n}"},{"name":"lint.functional_forms","kind":"fn","old":null,"new":"d8a44449685fbbb1","interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"lint","text":"/// The functional forms of the collection built-ins in `e` (`push(xs, x)`,\n/// `xs.sort()` not marked `mut`), by name, once per use.\nfn functional_forms(e: ast.Expr) -> List[String] {\n  here := match e {\n    ast.MutExpr(ast.MethodCall { .. }) => [],\n    ast.Call { callee: ast.Var(q), args } => if lint.old_arity(lint.call_name(q), len(args) - 1) {\n      [lint.call_name(q)]\n    } else {\n      []\n    },\n    ast.MethodCall { name, args, .. } => if lint.old_arity(name, len(args)) {\n      [name]\n    } else {\n      []\n    },\n    _ => [],\n  }\n  inner := match e {\n    ast.MutExpr(ast.MethodCall { recv, args, .. }) => [recv] + args,\n    _ => walk.kids(e),\n  }\n  here\n    + inner\n      .map(k -> lint.functional_forms(k))\n      .fold([], (a, b) -> a + b)\n}"},{"name":"lint.old_forms","kind":"fn","old":"9af0a9eaa684f6dc","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"lint","old_text":"/// The functional forms of the collection built-ins in `e` (`push(xs, x)`,\n/// `xs.sort()` not marked `mut`), by name, once per use.\nfn old_forms(e: ast.Expr) -> List[String] {\n  here := match e {\n    ast.MutExpr(ast.MethodCall { .. }) => [],\n    ast.Call { callee: ast.Var(q), args } => if lint.old_arity(lint.call_name(q), len(args) - 1) {\n      [lint.call_name(q)]\n    } else {\n      []\n    },\n    ast.MethodCall { name, args, .. } => if lint.old_arity(name, len(args)) {\n      [name]\n    } else {\n      []\n    },\n    _ => [],\n  }\n  inner := match e {\n    ast.MutExpr(ast.MethodCall { recv, args, .. }) => [recv] + args,\n    _ => walk.kids(e),\n  }\n  here + inner.map(k -> lint.old_forms(k)).fold([], (a, b) -> a + b)\n}"}],"renames":[{"from":"lint.old_forms","to":"lint.functional_forms","kind":"function"}],"references":["lint.collection_forms"]}
{"id":"fb8b5a5a907397b5","time":1795635053,"message":"rename lint.old_arity → lint.functional_arity","changes":[{"name":"lint.functional_forms","kind":"fn","old":"d8a44449685fbbb1","new":"81baa5c5f21b2548","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"lint","text":"/// The functional forms of the collection built-ins in `e` (`push(xs, x)`,\n/// `xs.sort()` not marked `mut`), by name, once per use.\nfn functional_forms(e: ast.Expr) -> List[String] {\n  here := match e {\n    ast.MutExpr(ast.MethodCall { .. }) => [],\n    ast.Call { callee: ast.Var(q), args } => if lint.functional_arity(lint.call_name(q), len(args) - 1) {\n      [lint.call_name(q)]\n    } else {\n      []\n    },\n    ast.MethodCall { name, args, .. } => if lint.functional_arity(name, len(args)) {\n      [name]\n    } else {\n      []\n    },\n    _ => [],\n  }\n  inner := match e {\n    ast.MutExpr(ast.MethodCall { recv, args, .. }) => [recv] + args,\n    _ => walk.kids(e),\n  }\n  here\n    + inner\n      .map(k -> lint.functional_forms(k))\n      .fold([], (a, b) -> a + b)\n}","old_text":"/// The functional forms of the collection built-ins in `e` (`push(xs, x)`,\n/// `xs.sort()` not marked `mut`), by name, once per use.\nfn functional_forms(e: ast.Expr) -> List[String] {\n  here := match e {\n    ast.MutExpr(ast.MethodCall { .. }) => [],\n    ast.Call { callee: ast.Var(q), args } => if lint.old_arity(lint.call_name(q), len(args) - 1) {\n      [lint.call_name(q)]\n    } else {\n      []\n    },\n    ast.MethodCall { name, args, .. } => if lint.old_arity(name, len(args)) {\n      [name]\n    } else {\n      []\n    },\n    _ => [],\n  }\n  inner := match e {\n    ast.MutExpr(ast.MethodCall { recv, args, .. }) => [recv] + args,\n    _ => walk.kids(e),\n  }\n  here\n    + inner\n      .map(k -> lint.functional_forms(k))\n      .fold([], (a, b) -> a + b)\n}"},{"name":"lint.functional_arity","kind":"fn","old":null,"new":"f05896e9f5aa688e","interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"lint","text":"/// Whether built-in `n` with `k` arguments after the list, dict or set is\n/// one of the functional forms (`push(xs, x)`: `k` is 1).\nfn functional_arity(n: String, k: Int) -> Bool {\n  match n {\n    \"push\" | \"sort_by\" | \"remove\" => k == 1,\n    \"sort\" | \"reverse\" => k == 0,\n    \"insert\" => k == 1 || k == 2,\n    _ => false,\n  }\n}"},{"name":"lint.assigned_back","kind":"fn","old":"901af6e7ac4ac30b","new":"67b66e09fa6d507f","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"lint","text":"/// `p = push(p, x)` (or `p = p.push(x)`) as `mut p.push(x)`, and likewise\n/// `insert`, `remove`, `sort` and `sort_by` assigned back to the variable\n/// or field they read. A call whose value is dropped (`xs.push(x)`, which\n/// changes nothing) also becomes the `mut` method.\nfn assigned_back(s: ast.Stmt) -> ast.Stmt {\n  match s {\n    ast.Assign { place, value } => if lint.place_like(place) {\n      match value {\n        ast.Call { callee: ast.Var(q), args: [first, ..rest] } => if first == place\n          && lint.back_form(lint.call_name(q), len(rest)) {\n          return ast.ExprStmt(ast.MutExpr(ast.MethodCall {\n            recv: place,\n            name: lint.call_name(q),\n            args: rest,\n          }))\n        },\n        ast.MethodCall { recv, name, args } => if recv == place && lint.back_form(name, len(args)) {\n          return ast.ExprStmt(\n            ast.MutExpr(ast.MethodCall { recv: place, name, args }),\n          )\n        },\n        _ => (),\n      }\n    },\n    ast.ExprStmt(ast.MethodCall { recv, name, args }) => if lint.place_like(recv) && lint.functional_arity(name, len(args)) {\n      return ast.ExprStmt(ast.MutExpr(ast.MethodCall { recv, name, args }))\n    },\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  s\n}","old_text":"/// `p = push(p, x)` (or `p = p.push(x)`) as `mut p.push(x)`, and likewise\n/// `insert`, `remove`, `sort` and `sort_by` assigned back to the variable\n/// or field they read. A call whose value is dropped (`xs.push(x)`, which\n/// changes nothing) also becomes the `mut` method.\nfn assigned_back(s: ast.Stmt) -> ast.Stmt {\n  match s {\n    ast.Assign { place, value } => if lint.place_like(place) {\n      match value {\n        ast.Call { callee: ast.Var(q), args: [first, ..rest] } => if first == place\n          && lint.back_form(lint.call_name(q), len(rest)) {\n          return ast.ExprStmt(ast.MutExpr(ast.MethodCall {\n            recv: place,\n            name: lint.call_name(q),\n            args: rest,\n          }))\n        },\n        ast.MethodCall { recv, name, args } => if recv == place && lint.back_form(name, len(args)) {\n          return ast.ExprStmt(\n            ast.MutExpr(ast.MethodCall { recv: place, name, args }),\n          )\n        },\n        _ => (),\n      }\n    },\n    ast.ExprStmt(ast.MethodCall { recv, name, args }) => if lint.place_like(recv) && lint.old_arity(name, len(args)) {\n      return ast.ExprStmt(ast.MutExpr(ast.MethodCall { recv, name, args }))\n    },\n    _ => (),\n  }\n  s\n}"},{"name":"lint.back_form","kind":"fn","old":"ef51d849d4a6b78d","new":"e6455ea9934564f6","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"lint","text":"/// The functional forms whose assignment back is a `mut` method. Not\n/// `reverse`, which strings have too: `s = s.reversed()`.\nfn back_form(n: String, k: Int) -> Bool {\n  lint.functional_arity(n, k) && n != \"reverse\"\n}","old_text":"/// The functional forms whose assignment back is a `mut` method. Not\n/// `reverse`, which strings have too: `s = s.reversed()`.\nfn back_form(n: String, k: Int) -> Bool {\n  lint.old_arity(n, k) && n != \"reverse\"\n}"},{"name":"lint.new_value","kind":"fn","old":"cc71e328ac763c46","new":"0e087f59d4c2888b","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"lint","text":"/// A functional form as the expression for its new value: `push(xs, x)` is\n/// `xs + [x]`, `sort(xs)` is `xs.sorted()`, `insert(d, k, v)` is a changed\n/// copy.\nfn new_value(e: ast.Expr) -> ast.Expr {\n  (n, first, rest, method) := match e {\n    ast.Call { callee: ast.Var(q), args: [first, ..rest] } => (lint.call_name(q), first, rest, false),\n    ast.MethodCall { recv, name, args } => (name, recv, args, true),\n    _ => return e,\n  }\n  if !lint.functional_arity(n, len(rest)) {\n    return e\n  }\n  match (n, rest) {\n    (\"push\", [x]) => ast.Binary {\n      op: ast.Add,\n      left: first,\n      right: ast.ListExpr([x]),\n    },\n    (\"sort\", []) => ast.MethodCall { recv: first, name: \"sorted\", args: [] },\n    (\"sort_by\", [k]) => ast.MethodCall { recv: first, name: \"sorted_by\", args: [k] },\n    (\"reverse\", []) => ast.MethodCall { recv: first, name: \"reversed\", args: [] },\n    _ => if method {\n      // a method `insert` of the program's own types: left alone\n      e\n    } else {\n      c := lint.fresh_copy(rest)\n      ast.Block { stmts: [\n        ast.VarDecl { name: c, ty: None, value: first },\n        ast.ExprStmt(ast.MutExpr(\n          ast.MethodCall { recv: ast.Var(c), name: n, args: rest },\n        )),\n      ], last: ast.Var(c) }\n    },\n  }\n}","old_text":"/// A functional form as the expression for its new value: `push(xs, x)` is\n/// `xs + [x]`, `sort(xs)` is `xs.sorted()`, `insert(d, k, v)` is a changed\n/// copy.\nfn new_value(e: ast.Expr) -> ast.Expr {\n  (n, first, rest, method) := match e {\n    ast.Call { callee: ast.Var(q), args: [first, ..rest] } => (lint.call_name(q), first, rest, false),\n    ast.MethodCall { recv, name, args } => (name, recv, args, true),\n    _ => return e,\n  }\n  if !lint.old_arity(n, len(rest)) {\n    return e\n  }\n  match (n, rest) {\n    (\"push\", [x]) => ast.Binary {\n      op: ast.Add,\n      left: first,\n      right: ast.ListExpr([x]),\n    },\n    (\"sort\", []) => ast.MethodCall { recv: first, name: \"sorted\", args: [] },\n    (\"sort_by\", [k]) => ast.MethodCall { recv: first, name: \"sorted_by\", args: [k] },\n    (\"reverse\", []) => ast.MethodCall { recv: first, name: \"reversed\", args: [] },\n    _ => if method {\n      // a method `insert` of the program's own types: left alone\n      e\n    } else {\n      c := lint.fresh_copy(rest)\n      ast.Block { stmts: [\n        ast.VarDecl { name: c, ty: None, value: first },\n        ast.ExprStmt(ast.MutExpr(\n          ast.MethodCall { recv: ast.Var(c), name: n, args: rest },\n        )),\n      ], last: ast.Var(c) }\n    },\n  }\n}"},{"name":"lint.call_name","kind":"fn","old":"ae94812d39b8f88a","new":"90374b5e3c2cfd71","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"lint","text":"/// A called function's name as the rules read it. A collection built-in\n/// stored as a module's trait method (`std.fs.remove`, an imported `Files`\n/// method) reads as the built-in (`remove`).\nfn call_name(q: String) -> String {\n  parts := split(q, \".\")\n  n := get(parts, len(parts) - 1) ?? q\n  if lint.functional_arity(n, 0)\n    || lint.functional_arity(n, 1)\n    || lint.functional_arity(n, 2) {\n    n\n  } else {\n    q\n  }\n}","old_text":"/// A called function's name as the rules read it. A collection built-in\n/// stored as a module's trait method (`std.fs.remove`, an imported `Files`\n/// method) reads as the built-in (`remove`).\nfn call_name(q: String) -> String {\n  parts := split(q, \".\")\n  n := get(parts, len(parts) - 1) ?? q\n  if lint.old_arity(n, 0)\n    || lint.old_arity(n, 1)\n    || lint.old_arity(n, 2) {\n    n\n  } else {\n    q\n  }\n}"},{"name":"lint.old_arity","kind":"fn","old":"a1b542498ebc05f1","new":null,"interface_changed":true,"affected":[],"module":"lint","old_text":"/// Whether built-in `n` with `k` arguments after the list, dict or set is\n/// one of the functional forms (`push(xs, x)`: `k` is 1).\nfn old_arity(n: String, k: Int) -> Bool {\n  match n {\n    \"push\" | \"sort_by\" | \"remove\" => k == 1,\n    \"sort\" | \"reverse\" => k == 0,\n    \"insert\" => k == 1 || k == 2,\n    _ => false,\n  }\n}"}],"renames":[{"from":"lint.old_arity","to":"lint.functional_arity","kind":"function"}],"references":["lint.functional_forms","lint.assigned_back","lint.back_form","lint.new_value","lint.call_name"]}
{"id":"f00f447f73ab4da9","time":1795633802,"message":"edit","changes":[{"name":"termination.use ast","kind":"use","old":"11ae506670d6badc","new":"2055c745bb59aa19","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"// termination: whether each function always finishes, by structural\n// recursion, a measure the solver checks, or loop bounds.\nfrom ast use FnDecl, TypeDecl, TypeExpr, Expr, Stmt, Pattern, Param, ImplDecl,\n  TraitDecl, Named, FnType, UnitType, Refined, UnionType, Alias, RecordBody,\n  SumBody, NoPayload, Positional, RecordPayload, MemberType, IntLit, FloatLit,\n  StrLit, Var, Hole, CtorExpr, Call, MethodCall, FieldOf, Lambda, Binary,\n  MatchExpr, MutExpr, Block, MockExpr, Return, Try, TupleExpr, ListExpr, Except,\n  Div, Mod, Sub, Less, LessEq, Greater, GreaterEq, NotEqual, Equal, Let,\n  VarDecl, Assign, While, For, Loop, ExprStmt, Assert, Invariant, Decreases,\n  ComptimeFor, Wild, Bind, CtorPattern, ListPat, TuplePat, CondPat, OrPat,\n  ForPat, NoPats, PositionalPats, RecordPats, TypePats","old_text":"from ast use FnDecl, TypeDecl, TypeExpr, Expr, Stmt, Pattern, Param, ImplDecl,\n  TraitDecl, Named, FnType, UnitType, Refined, UnionType, Alias, RecordBody,\n  SumBody, NoPayload, Positional, RecordPayload, MemberType, IntLit, FloatLit,\n  StrLit, Var, Hole, CtorExpr, Call, MethodCall, FieldOf, Lambda, Binary,\n  MatchExpr, MutExpr, Block, MockExpr, Return, Try, TupleExpr, ListExpr, Except,\n  Div, Mod, Sub, Less, LessEq, Greater, GreaterEq, NotEqual, Equal, Let,\n  VarDecl, Assign, While, For, Loop, ExprStmt, Assert, Invariant, Decreases,\n  ComptimeFor, Wild, Bind, CtorPattern, ListPat, TuplePat, CondPat, OrPat,\n  ForPat, NoPats, PositionalPats, RecordPats, TypePats"},{"name":"termination.Termination","kind":"type","old":"71de945a9696e7b6","new":"6d7982fb9f5f216c","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"/// A function's termination verdict.\n/// - `Proven(how)`.\n/// - `Assumed(names)`: it finishes if the named `terminates` functions do.\n/// - `Unknown(why)`.\npub type Termination =\n  | Proven(String)\n  | Assumed(List[String])\n  | Unknown(String)","old_text":"/// Whether a function always finishes: `Proven` (how), `Assumed` (if the\n/// functions marked `terminates` named do), or `Unknown` (why not).\npub type Termination =\n  | Proven(String)\n  | Assumed(List[String])\n  | Unknown(String)"},{"name":"termination.Analysis","kind":"type","old":"94e173d0a056ba96","new":"4671e76199e32fa0","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"/// The verdicts by function name (`Type.method` for an implementation's\n/// method), and the functions that call themselves, directly or through\n/// others. `transparent`: the functions a contract may see through, `true`\n/// when that relies on an assumed finish.\npub type Analysis = {\n  status: Dict[String, termination.Termination],\n  recursive: Set[String],\n  transparent: Dict[String, Bool],\n  // the recursive functions a contract may unfold: they call only\n  // themselves, finish, and fail nowhere else\n  unfold: Set[String] = Set[String] {},\n}","old_text":"/// The verdicts by function name (`Type.method` for an implementation's\n/// method), the functions that call themselves (directly or through\n/// others), and those a contract may see through (finishing only assumed:\n/// `true`).\npub type Analysis = {\n  status: Dict[String, termination.Termination],\n  recursive: Set[String],\n  transparent: Dict[String, Bool],\n  // the recursive functions a contract may unfold (calling only\n  // themselves, finishing, failing nowhere else)\n  unfold: Set[String] = Set[String] {},\n}"},{"name":"termination.Ctx","kind":"type","old":"7b0f5f98573332ff","new":"0a28c2d0df03edf2","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"/// The program as the verifier sees it, and how to run the solver.\npub type Ctx = {\n  fns: Dict[String, ast.FnDecl],\n  types: Dict[String, ast.TypeDecl],\n  sigs: List[smt.BuiltinSig],\n  methods: smt.Methods,\n  scratch: String,\n  solver: String,\n  // a run over the program, to ask the encoder for a type's refinements\n  // and the variables an expression changes\n  base: smt.Vc,\n}","old_text":"/// The program as the verifier sees it, and how to run the solver.\npub type Ctx = {\n  fns: Dict[String, ast.FnDecl],\n  types: Dict[String, ast.TypeDecl],\n  sigs: List[smt.BuiltinSig],\n  methods: smt.Methods,\n  scratch: String,\n  solver: String,\n  // a run over them, for what asks the encoder (a type's refinements, the\n  // variables an expression changes)\n  base: smt.Vc,\n}"},{"name":"termination.context","kind":"fn","old":"c694c23e3322523d","new":"434593dcfb2ecd01","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"pub fn context(\n  fns: Dict[String, ast.FnDecl],\n  types: Dict[String, ast.TypeDecl],\n  sigs: List[smt.BuiltinSig],\n  methods: smt.Methods,\n  scratch: String,\n  solver: String,\n) -> termination.Ctx {\n  // the types that reach a refinement, found once for every run\n  with_refined := smt.Methods { ..methods, refined_types: Some(smt.refined_types(types)) }\n  termination.Ctx {\n    fns,\n    types,\n    sigs,\n    methods: with_refined,\n    scratch,\n    solver,\n    base: smt.new_vc(fns, types, sigs, with_refined),\n  }\n}","old_text":"/// The context of `analyze`.\npub fn context(\n  fns: Dict[String, ast.FnDecl],\n  types: Dict[String, ast.TypeDecl],\n  sigs: List[smt.BuiltinSig],\n  methods: smt.Methods,\n  scratch: String,\n  solver: String,\n) -> termination.Ctx {\n  // (the types reaching a refinement found once, for every run's `refined`)\n  with_refined := smt.Methods { ..methods, refined_types: Some(smt.refined_types(types)) }\n  termination.Ctx {\n    fns,\n    types,\n    sigs,\n    methods: with_refined,\n    scratch,\n    solver,\n    base: smt.new_vc(fns, types, sigs, with_refined),\n  }\n}"},{"name":"termination.Node","kind":"type","old":"fbf85987d997c528","new":"ca87365ef6288a26","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"/// A call graph node: a function, an implementation's method, or a trait\n/// method (which stands for every implementation). `decl` is checked for\n/// recursion, `body` for loops.\ntype Node = {\n  decl: Option[ast.FnDecl],\n  calls: Set[String],\n  body: Option[ast.FnDecl],\n}","old_text":"/// A node of the call graph: a function, an implementation's method, or a\n/// trait method (which may be any implementation's). `decl`: a function's\n/// declaration (for recursion); `body`: the code whose loops are checked.\ntype Node = {\n  decl: Option[ast.FnDecl],\n  calls: Set[String],\n  body: Option[ast.FnDecl],\n}"},{"name":"termination.short","kind":"fn","old":"7b48ebfa3d7ec22a","new":"b71390505f6c60e3","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"fn short(n: String) -> String {\n  parts := split(n, \".\")\n  get(parts, len(parts) - 1) ?? n\n}","old_text":"/// The last part of a dotted name.\nfn short(n: String) -> String {\n  parts := split(n, \".\")\n  get(parts, len(parts) - 1) ?? n\n}"},{"name":"termination.trait_node","kind":"fn","old":"2463d14fda2500b7","new":"d7f92a72962a9a4b","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"/// The node of `Trait::m`, a call through one trait. It reaches the\n/// implementations of `m`.\nfn trait_node(m: String) -> String {\n  match index_of(m, \"::\") {\n    Some(k) => \"trait method \" + byte_slice(m, k + 2, byte_len(m)),\n    None => \"trait method \" + m,\n  }\n}","old_text":"/// `Trait::m` (a call through one trait) reaches the implementations of `m`.\nfn trait_node(m: String) -> String {\n  match index_of(m, \"::\") {\n    Some(k) => \"trait method \" + byte_slice(m, k + 2, byte_len(m)),\n    None => \"trait method \" + m,\n  }\n}"},{"name":"termination.shown_node","kind":"fn","old":"2f6c697520cc7b1f","new":"26d0e15a4a53ebe4","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"/// A trait method's node by its shown name (`next` for `core.iter.next`).\nfn shown_node(n: String) -> String {\n  if starts_with(n, \"trait method \") {\n    termination.short(byte_slice(n, 13, byte_len(n)))\n  } else {\n    n\n  }\n}","old_text":"/// A trait method's node by the name it is shown with (`next`, not\n/// `core.iter.next`), or the name itself.\nfn shown_node(n: String) -> String {\n  if starts_with(n, \"trait method \") {\n    termination.short(byte_slice(n, 13, byte_len(n)))\n  } else {\n    n\n  }\n}"},{"name":"termination.is_method","kind":"fn","old":"b6c90a66c0d91ea9","new":"b309e38bb3c270f9","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"/// Whether `n` is a trait method or a call through one trait (`Trait::m`).\n/// Methods of core's code modules (`map`, `get`, `len`) are builtins. A\n/// type's own methods are known by qualified names, which no call uses.\nfn is_method(ctx: termination.Ctx, n: String) -> Bool {\n  contains(n, \"::\")\n    || ctx.methods.traits.any(\n      t -> !contains(ctx.methods.code_traits, t.name)\n        && t.methods.any(m -> m.decl.name == n),\n    )\n}","old_text":"/// Whether `n` is a method: of a trait (not of core's code modules: `map`,\n/// `get` and `len` are the builtins'), or a call through one trait\n/// (`Trait::m`). (A\n/// type's own methods are known to Rust's analysis by their qualified\n/// names, which no call names.)\nfn is_method(ctx: termination.Ctx, n: String) -> Bool {\n  contains(n, \"::\")\n    || ctx.methods.traits.any(\n      t -> !contains(ctx.methods.code_traits, t.name)\n        && t.methods.any(m -> m.decl.name == n),\n    )\n}"},{"name":"termination.head","kind":"fn","old":"24af0d35922deddb","new":"ce5a049e56c17505","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"/// The head of a type: `List` for `List[Int]`.\nfn head(t: ast.TypeExpr) -> String {\n  match t {\n    ast.Named { name, .. } => name,\n    _ => \"\",\n  }\n}","old_text":"/// The head of a type (`List` of `List[Int]`).\nfn head(t: ast.TypeExpr) -> String {\n  match t {\n    ast.Named { name, .. } => name,\n    _ => \"\",\n  }\n}"},{"name":"termination.trait_of","kind":"fn","old":"08146d1a60c59aa5","new":"dcdf946ffc833a84","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"fn trait_of(ctx: termination.Ctx, imp: ast.ImplDecl) -> Option[ast.TraitDecl] {\n  get(ctx.methods.traits.filter(\n    t -> t.name == imp.trait_name\n      || ends_with(imp.trait_name, \".\" + t.name),\n  ), 0)\n}","old_text":"/// The trait an implementation is of.\nfn trait_of(ctx: termination.Ctx, imp: ast.ImplDecl) -> Option[ast.TraitDecl] {\n  get(ctx.methods.traits.filter(\n    t -> t.name == imp.trait_name\n      || ends_with(imp.trait_name, \".\" + t.name),\n  ), 0)\n}"},{"name":"termination.impl_label","kind":"fn","old":"c2871f18b90caec6","new":"ae84f7e7651f7eac","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"/// An implementation method's label in `verify` output. The trait is named\n/// too when the type has a method of that name of its own or from another\n/// trait: `Item.describe (Log)`.\npub fn impl_label(ctx: termination.Ctx, imp: ast.ImplDecl, m: String) -> String {\n  h := termination.head(imp.for_type)\n  base := text.type_text(imp.for_type) + \".\" + termination.short(m)\n  own := ctx.methods.own_types.any(o -> o.0 == h && o.1 == m)\n  traits := ctx.methods.traits.filter(\n    t -> t.methods.any(x -> x.decl.name == m)\n      && ctx.methods.impls.any(\n        i -> (i.trait_name == t.name\n            || ends_with(i.trait_name, \".\" + t.name))\n          && termination.head(i.for_type) == h,\n      ),\n  )\n  if imp.trait_name != \"\" && (own || len(traits) > 1) {\n    base + \" (\" + termination.short(imp.trait_name) + \")\"\n  } else {\n    base\n  }\n}","old_text":"/// The label of an implementation's method, as `verify` shows it; the\n/// trait is named too when the type has a method of that name of its own,\n/// or from another trait: `Item.describe (Log)`.\npub fn impl_label(ctx: termination.Ctx, imp: ast.ImplDecl, m: String) -> String {\n  h := termination.head(imp.for_type)\n  base := text.type_text(imp.for_type) + \".\" + termination.short(m)\n  own := ctx.methods.own_types.any(o -> o.0 == h && o.1 == m)\n  traits := ctx.methods.traits.filter(\n    t -> t.methods.any(x -> x.decl.name == m)\n      && ctx.methods.impls.any(\n        i -> (i.trait_name == t.name\n            || ends_with(i.trait_name, \".\" + t.name))\n          && termination.head(i.for_type) == h,\n      ),\n  )\n  if imp.trait_name != \"\" && (own || len(traits) > 1) {\n    base + \" (\" + termination.short(imp.trait_name) + \")\"\n  } else {\n    base\n  }\n}"},{"name":"termination.Calls","kind":"type","old":"ec6a8cac2b944c7b","new":"0eb47ff2f7b9cb77","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"// ---- calls ----\n\n/// The call-collecting walk: the calls found, the names bound around the\n/// expression, and the trait method being implemented (`\"\"` if none).\ntype Calls = { out: Set[String], scopes: List[Set[String]], own: String }","old_text":"// ---- calls ----\n\n/// The walk collecting calls: what is found, the names bound around the\n/// expression, and the trait method whose implementation this is (`\"\"`).\ntype Calls = { out: Set[String], scopes: List[Set[String]], own: String }"},{"name":"termination.calls_within","kind":"fn","old":"ecfecc8811f615fa","new":"c1d4aa1f78b11e3a","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"/// The functions and trait methods `e` calls or passes as values. `locals`\n/// are names bound outside `e`. In an implementation of the trait method\n/// `own`, a call of it on a field of `self` recurses on a smaller value\n/// and is left out.\nfn calls_within(\n  ctx: termination.Ctx,\n  e: ast.Expr,\n  locals: List[String],\n  own: String,\n) -> Set[String] {\n  mut st := termination.Calls {\n    out: Set[String] {},\n    scopes: [set(locals)],\n    own,\n  }\n  termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, e)\n  st.out\n}","old_text":"/// The functions and trait methods `e` calls or passes as values. `locals`\n/// are names bound outside `e`; `own` (the trait node, or `\"\"`): in an\n/// implementation of that trait method, a call of it on a field of `self`\n/// is recursion on a smaller value, left out.\nfn calls_within(\n  ctx: termination.Ctx,\n  e: ast.Expr,\n  locals: List[String],\n  own: String,\n) -> Set[String] {\n  mut st := termination.Calls {\n    out: Set[String] {},\n    scopes: [set(locals)],\n    own,\n  }\n  termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, e)\n  st.out\n}"},{"name":"termination.self_field","kind":"fn","old":"729b503e407d6a37","new":"8232cf39e04bbb3d","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"/// `self.a.b`: a field, or a field of a field, of `self`.\nfn self_field(e: ast.Expr) -> Bool {\n  match e {\n    ast.FieldOf { base, .. } => match base {\n      ast.Var(v) => v == \"self\",\n      _ => termination.self_field(base),\n    },\n    _ => false,\n  }\n}","old_text":"/// `self.a.b`: a field (of a field) of `self`.\nfn self_field(e: ast.Expr) -> Bool {\n  match e {\n    ast.FieldOf { base, .. } => match base {\n      ast.Var(v) => v == \"self\",\n      _ => termination.self_field(base),\n    },\n    _ => false,\n  }\n}"},{"name":"termination.pattern_binds","kind":"fn","old":"8cc0833324adce81","new":"52c60bfe5ea579a7","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"fn pattern_binds(p: ast.Pattern) -> List[String] {\n  match p {\n    ast.Bind(n) => [n],\n    ast.CtorPattern { args, .. } => match args {\n      ast.PositionalPats(ps) | ast.TypePats(ps) => fold(\n        ps.map(x -> termination.pattern_binds(x)),\n        [],\n        (a, b) -> a + b,\n      ),\n      ast.RecordPats { fields, .. } => fold(\n        fields.map(f -> termination.pattern_binds(f.1)),\n        [],\n        (a, b) -> a + b,\n      ),\n      ast.NoPats => [],\n    },\n    ast.ListPat { items, rest } => fold(\n        items.map(x -> termination.pattern_binds(x)),\n        [],\n        (a, b) -> a + b,\n      )\n      + match rest {\n        Some(r) => [r],\n        None => [],\n      },\n    ast.TuplePat(ps) | ast.OrPat(ps) => fold(\n      ps.map(x -> termination.pattern_binds(x)),\n      [],\n      (a, b) -> a + b,\n    ),\n    ast.ForPat { arm, each, .. } => termination.pattern_binds(arm) + termination.pattern_binds(each),\n    _ => [],\n  }\n}","old_text":"/// The names a pattern binds.\nfn pattern_binds(p: ast.Pattern) -> List[String] {\n  match p {\n    ast.Bind(n) => [n],\n    ast.CtorPattern { args, .. } => match args {\n      ast.PositionalPats(ps) | ast.TypePats(ps) => fold(\n        ps.map(x -> termination.pattern_binds(x)),\n        [],\n        (a, b) -> a + b,\n      ),\n      ast.RecordPats { fields, .. } => fold(\n        fields.map(f -> termination.pattern_binds(f.1)),\n        [],\n        (a, b) -> a + b,\n      ),\n      ast.NoPats => [],\n    },\n    ast.ListPat { items, rest } => fold(\n        items.map(x -> termination.pattern_binds(x)),\n        [],\n        (a, b) -> a + b,\n      )\n      + match rest {\n        Some(r) => [r],\n        None => [],\n      },\n    ast.TuplePat(ps) | ast.OrPat(ps) => fold(\n      ps.map(x -> termination.pattern_binds(x)),\n      [],\n      (a, b) -> a + b,\n    ),\n    ast.ForPat { arm, each, .. } => termination.pattern_binds(arm) + termination.pattern_binds(each),\n    _ => [],\n  }\n}"},{"name":"termination.calls_in","kind":"fn","old":"db89c51d26e71b82","new":"8d227eea6a079c25","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"fn calls_in(mut st: termination.Calls, ctx: termination.Ctx, e: ast.Expr) {\n  if termination.is_setting(e) {\n    return\n  }\n  match e {\n    // a function called, or passed as a value that may be called\n    ast.Var(n) => termination.call_name(mut st, ctx, n),\n    ast.MethodCall { recv, name, args } => {\n      smaller := st.own != \"\"\n        && termination.trait_node(name) == st.own\n        && termination.self_field(recv)\n      // a method a type has of its own is that type's, not the function of\n      // the same name: `k.bump()` with `impl Counter { fn bump }`\n      own := ctx.methods.own_types.any(t -> t.1 == name)\n      if !smaller && !own {\n        termination.call_name(mut st, ctx, name)\n      }\n      termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, recv)\n      for a in args {\n        termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, a)\n      }\n    },\n    ast.Lambda { params, body } => termination.scoped(mut st, ctx, params.map(p -> p.name), body),\n    ast.MatchExpr { scrutinee, arms, .. } => {\n      termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, scrutinee)\n      for a in arms {\n        for x in walk.pattern_kids(a.pat) {\n          termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, x)\n        }\n        termination.scoped(\n          mut st,\n          ctx,\n          termination.pattern_binds(a.pat),\n          a.body,\n        )\n      }\n    },\n    ast.Block { stmts, last } => {\n      // each binding is visible from the next statement on\n      mut st.scopes.push(Set[String] {})\n      for s in stmts {\n        match s {\n          ast.ComptimeFor { .. } => (),\n          ast.Let { pat, value, .. } => {\n            termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, value)\n            for x in walk.pattern_kids(pat) {\n              termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, x)\n            }\n            termination.bind_here(\n              mut st,\n              termination.pattern_binds(pat),\n            )\n          },\n          ast.VarDecl { name, value, .. } => {\n            termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, value)\n            termination.bind_here(mut st, [name])\n          },\n          ast.For { pat, iter, body } => {\n            termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, iter)\n            for x in walk.pattern_kids(pat) {\n              termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, x)\n            }\n            termination.scoped(\n              mut st,\n              ctx,\n              termination.pattern_binds(pat),\n              body,\n            )\n          },\n          ast.Assign { place, value } => {\n            termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, place)\n            termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, value)\n          },\n          ast.While { cond, body } => {\n            termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, cond)\n            termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, body)\n          },\n          ast.Loop(x) | ast.ExprStmt(x) | ast.Assert(x) | ast.Invariant(x) | ast.Decreases(x) => termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, x),\n          _ => (),\n        }\n      }\n      termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, last)\n      st.scopes = take(st.scopes, len(st.scopes) - 1)\n    },\n    _ => {\n      for k in walk.kids(e) {\n        termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, k)\n      }\n    },\n  }\n}","old_text":"fn calls_in(mut st: termination.Calls, ctx: termination.Ctx, e: ast.Expr) {\n  if termination.is_setting(e) {\n    return\n  }\n  match e {\n    // a function called, or passed as a value (it may be called)\n    ast.Var(n) => termination.call_name(mut st, ctx, n),\n    ast.MethodCall { recv, name, args } => {\n      smaller := st.own != \"\"\n        && termination.trait_node(name) == st.own\n        && termination.self_field(recv)\n      // (a method a type has of its own is that type's, not the function\n      // of the same name: `k.bump()` with `impl Counter { fn bump }`)\n      own := ctx.methods.own_types.any(t -> t.1 == name)\n      if !smaller && !own {\n        termination.call_name(mut st, ctx, name)\n      }\n      termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, recv)\n      for a in args {\n        termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, a)\n      }\n    },\n    ast.Lambda { params, body } => termination.scoped(mut st, ctx, params.map(p -> p.name), body),\n    ast.MatchExpr { scrutinee, arms, .. } => {\n      termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, scrutinee)\n      for a in arms {\n        for x in walk.pattern_kids(a.pat) {\n          termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, x)\n        }\n        termination.scoped(\n          mut st,\n          ctx,\n          termination.pattern_binds(a.pat),\n          a.body,\n        )\n      }\n    },\n    ast.Block { stmts, last } => {\n      // each binding is visible from the next statement on\n      mut st.scopes.push(Set[String] {})\n      for s in stmts {\n        match s {\n          ast.ComptimeFor { .. } => (),\n          ast.Let { pat, value, .. } => {\n            termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, value)\n            for x in walk.pattern_kids(pat) {\n              termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, x)\n            }\n            termination.bind_here(\n              mut st,\n              termination.pattern_binds(pat),\n            )\n          },\n          ast.VarDecl { name, value, .. } => {\n            termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, value)\n            termination.bind_here(mut st, [name])\n          },\n          ast.For { pat, iter, body } => {\n            termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, iter)\n            for x in walk.pattern_kids(pat) {\n              termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, x)\n            }\n            termination.scoped(\n              mut st,\n              ctx,\n              termination.pattern_binds(pat),\n              body,\n            )\n          },\n          ast.Assign { place, value } => {\n            termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, place)\n            termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, value)\n          },\n          ast.While { cond, body } => {\n            termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, cond)\n            termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, body)\n          },\n          ast.Loop(x) | ast.ExprStmt(x) | ast.Assert(x) | ast.Invariant(x) | ast.Decreases(x) => termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, x),\n          _ => (),\n        }\n      }\n      termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, last)\n      st.scopes = take(st.scopes, len(st.scopes) - 1)\n    },\n    _ => {\n      for k in walk.kids(e) {\n        termination.calls_in(mut st, ctx, k)\n      }\n    },\n  }\n}"},{"name":"termination.preorder","kind":"fn","old":"57e526f55cbf9ec8","new":"f396aa3990451cb5","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"// ---- loops ----\n\n/// Every expression in `e`, each before its subexpressions.\nfn preorder(e: ast.Expr) -> List[ast.Expr] {\n  mut out := []\n  mut todo := [e]\n  while len(todo) > 0 {\n    x := get(todo, len(todo) - 1) ?? e\n    todo = take(todo, len(todo) - 1)\n    mut out.push(x)\n    todo += walk.kids(x).reversed()\n  }\n  out\n}","old_text":"// ---- loops ----\n\n/// Every expression in `e`, each before the ones inside it.\nfn preorder(e: ast.Expr) -> List[ast.Expr] {\n  mut out := []\n  mut todo := [e]\n  while len(todo) > 0 {\n    x := get(todo, len(todo) - 1) ?? e\n    todo = take(todo, len(todo) - 1)\n    mut out.push(x)\n    todo += walk.kids(x).reversed()\n  }\n  out\n}"},{"name":"termination.statements","kind":"fn","old":"5050995166f0680b","new":"7dcef2bc0c52877b","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"fn statements(e: ast.Expr) -> List[ast.Stmt] {\n  mut out := []\n  for x in termination.preorder(e) {\n    match x {\n      ast.Block { stmts, .. } => {\n        out += stmts\n      },\n      _ => (),\n    }\n  }\n  out\n}","old_text":"/// The statements of every block in `e`.\nfn statements(e: ast.Expr) -> List[ast.Stmt] {\n  mut out := []\n  for x in termination.preorder(e) {\n    match x {\n      ast.Block { stmts, .. } => {\n        out += stmts\n      },\n      _ => (),\n    }\n  }\n  out\n}"},{"name":"termination.Piece","kind":"type","old":"daf78e22d7f7b054","new":"40b68545e7d1b218","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"// ---- structural recursion ----\n\n/// For a variable: the parameters it is a piece of or equal to, and those\n/// it is a strictly smaller piece of.\ntype Piece = { within: Set[Int], smaller: Set[Int] }","old_text":"// ---- structural recursion ----\n\n/// For a variable: the parameters it is a piece of (or equal to), and those\n/// it is a strictly smaller piece of.\ntype Piece = { within: Set[Int], smaller: Set[Int] }"},{"name":"termination.Structural","kind":"type","old":"adbc25041a57ed50","new":"f4c71cf0dbb63288","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"/// The recursive-call walk: the function's names as called, the variables\n/// assigned, and for each recursive call the parameters whose argument is\n/// smaller.\ntype Structural = {\n  names: Set[String],\n  assigned: Set[String],\n  calls: List[Set[Int]],\n}","old_text":"/// The walk looking at recursive calls: the function's names (as called),\n/// the variables assigned, and for each recursive call the parameters whose\n/// argument is smaller.\ntype Structural = {\n  names: Set[String],\n  assigned: Set[String],\n  calls: List[Set[Int]],\n}"},{"name":"termination.bind_piece","kind":"fn","old":"6fe11937dbeca8d7","new":"91392f8c8a0e71e9","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"/// Binds the variables of `p` matched against `scrut`. `depth > 0` means\n/// inside a constructor or list, so a strictly smaller piece.\nfn bind_piece(\n  st: termination.Structural,\n  p: ast.Pattern,\n  scrut: Option[ast.Expr],\n  whole: termination.Piece,\n  depth: Int,\n  mut vars: Dict[String, termination.Piece],\n) {\n  match p {\n    ast.Bind(x) => {\n      pc := if contains(st.assigned, x) {\n        termination.no_piece()\n      } else if depth > 0 {\n        termination.Piece {\n          within: whole.within,\n          smaller: whole.within,\n        }\n      } else {\n        whole\n      }\n      mut vars.insert(x, pc)\n    },\n    ast.TuplePat(ps) => {\n      tuple := match scrut {\n        Some(ast.TupleExpr(es)) => if len(es) == len(ps) && depth == 0 {\n          Some(es)\n        } else {\n          None\n        },\n        _ => None,\n      }\n      match tuple {\n        Some(es) => {\n          for (k, q) in enumerate(ps) {\n            e := get(es, k) ?? ast.Var(\"\")\n            w := termination.piece(e, vars)\n            termination.bind_piece(st, q, Some(e), w, 0, mut vars)\n          }\n        },\n        None => {\n          for q in ps {\n            termination.bind_piece(\n              st,\n              q,\n              None,\n              whole,\n              depth,\n              mut vars,\n            )\n          }\n        },\n      }\n    },\n    ast.ListPat { items, rest } => {\n      for q in items {\n        termination.bind_piece(\n          st,\n          q,\n          None,\n          whole,\n          depth + 1,\n          mut vars,\n        )\n      }\n      match rest {\n        Some(r) => termination.bind_piece(\n          st,\n          ast.Bind(r),\n          None,\n          whole,\n          depth + 1,\n          mut vars,\n        ),\n        None => (),\n      }\n    },\n    ast.CtorPattern { args, .. } => match args {\n      ast.PositionalPats(ps) | ast.TypePats(ps) => {\n        for q in ps {\n          termination.bind_piece(\n            st,\n            q,\n            None,\n            whole,\n            depth + 1,\n            mut vars,\n          )\n        }\n      },\n      ast.RecordPats { fields, .. } => {\n        for (_, q) in fields {\n          termination.bind_piece(\n            st,\n            q,\n            None,\n            whole,\n            depth + 1,\n            mut vars,\n          )\n        }\n      },\n      ast.NoPats => (),\n    },\n    ast.OrPat(alts) => {\n      // every alternative binds the same names: keep what holds in all\n      mut all := None\n      for a in alts {\n        mut v := vars\n        termination.bind_piece(st, a, scrut, whole, depth, mut v)\n        all = Some(match all {\n          None => v,\n          Some(prev) => {\n            mut both := Dict[String, termination.Piece] {}\n            for (k, p0) in items(prev) {\n              q := get(v, k) ?? termination.no_piece()\n              mut both.insert(\n                k,\n                termination.Piece {\n                  within: intersection(p0.within, q.within),\n                  smaller: intersection(p0.smaller, q.smaller),\n                },\n              )\n            }\n            both\n          },\n        })\n      }\n      match all {\n        Some(a) => {\n          vars = a\n        },\n        None => (),\n      }\n    },\n    _ => (),\n  }\n}","old_text":"/// Bind the variables of `p` matched against `scrut`. `depth` > 0 means\n/// inside a constructor or list: a strictly smaller piece.\nfn bind_piece(\n  st: termination.Structural,\n  p: ast.Pattern,\n  scrut: Option[ast.Expr],\n  whole: termination.Piece,\n  depth: Int,\n  mut vars: Dict[String, termination.Piece],\n) {\n  match p {\n    ast.Bind(x) => {\n      pc := if contains(st.assigned, x) {\n        termination.no_piece()\n      } else if depth > 0 {\n        termination.Piece {\n          within: whole.within,\n          smaller: whole.within,\n        }\n      } else {\n        whole\n      }\n      mut vars.insert(x, pc)\n    },\n    ast.TuplePat(ps) => {\n      tuple := match scrut {\n        Some(ast.TupleExpr(es)) => if len(es) == len(ps) && depth == 0 {\n          Some(es)\n        } else {\n          None\n        },\n        _ => None,\n      }\n      match tuple {\n        Some(es) => {\n          for (k, q) in enumerate(ps) {\n            e := get(es, k) ?? ast.Var(\"\")\n            w := termination.piece(e, vars)\n            termination.bind_piece(st, q, Some(e), w, 0, mut vars)\n          }\n        },\n        None => {\n          for q in ps {\n            termination.bind_piece(\n              st,\n              q,\n              None,\n              whole,\n              depth,\n              mut vars,\n            )\n          }\n        },\n      }\n    },\n    ast.ListPat { items, rest } => {\n      for q in items {\n        termination.bind_piece(\n          st,\n          q,\n          None,\n          whole,\n          depth + 1,\n          mut vars,\n        )\n      }\n      match rest {\n        Some(r) => termination.bind_piece(\n          st,\n          ast.Bind(r),\n          None,\n          whole,\n          depth + 1,\n          mut vars,\n        ),\n        None => (),\n      }\n    },\n    ast.CtorPattern { args, .. } => match args {\n      ast.PositionalPats(ps) | ast.TypePats(ps) => {\n        for q in ps {\n          termination.bind_piece(\n            st,\n            q,\n            None,\n            whole,\n            depth + 1,\n            mut vars,\n          )\n        }\n      },\n      ast.RecordPats { fields, .. } => {\n        for (_, q) in fields {\n          termination.bind_piece(\n            st,\n            q,\n            None,\n            whole,\n            depth + 1,\n            mut vars,\n          )\n        }\n      },\n      ast.NoPats => (),\n    },\n    ast.OrPat(alts) => {\n      // every alternative binds the same names; keep what holds in all\n      mut all := None\n      for a in alts {\n        mut v := vars\n        termination.bind_piece(st, a, scrut, whole, depth, mut v)\n        all = Some(match all {\n          None => v,\n          Some(prev) => {\n            mut both := Dict[String, termination.Piece] {}\n            for (k, p0) in items(prev) {\n              q := get(v, k) ?? termination.no_piece()\n              mut both.insert(\n                k,\n                termination.Piece {\n                  within: intersection(p0.within, q.within),\n                  smaller: intersection(p0.smaller, q.smaller),\n                },\n              )\n            }\n            both\n          },\n        })\n      }\n      match all {\n        Some(a) => {\n          vars = a\n        },\n        None => (),\n      }\n    },\n    _ => (),\n  }\n}"},{"name":"termination.struct_expr","kind":"fn","old":"6631bf41ce9234e0","new":"25c4b4a945384005","interface_changed":false,"affected":[],"module":"termination","text":"fn struct_expr(\n  mut st: termination.Structural,\n  e: ast.Expr,\n  vars: Dict[String, termination.Piece],\n) {\n  match e {\n    ast.Call { callee, args } => {\n      match callee {\n        ast.Var(n) => if contains(st.names, n) {\n          termination.struct_call(mut st, args, vars)\n        },\n        _ => (),\n      }\n      termination.struct_expr(mut st, callee, vars)\n      for a in args {\n        termination.struct_expr(mut st, a, vars)\n      }\n    },\n    ast.MethodCall { recv, name, args } => {\n      if contains(st.names, name) {\n        termination.struct_call(mut st, [recv] + args, vars)\n      }\n      termination.struct_expr(mut st, recv, vars)\n      for a in args {\n        termination.struct_expr(mut st, a, vars)\n      }\n    },\n    ast.MatchExpr { scrutinee, binding, arms } => {\n      termination.struct_expr(mut st, scrutinee, vars)\n      whole := termination.piece(scrutinee, vars)\n      for a in arms {\n        mut v := vars\n        // a recursive call in a `where` pattern counts too\n        termination.pattern_conds(mut st, a.pat, vars)\n        match binding {\n          Some(n) => mut v.insert(n, whole),\n          None => (),\n        }\n        termination.bind_piece(\n          st,\n          a.pat,\n          Some(scrutinee),\n          whole,\n          0,\n          mut v,\n        )\n        termination.struct_expr(mut st, a.body, v)\n      }\n    },\n    ast.Lambda { params, body } => {\n      mut v := vars\n      for p in params {\n        mut v.remove(p.name)\n      }\n      termination.struct_expr(mut st, body, v)\n    },\n    ast.Block { stmts, last } => {\n      mut v := vars\n      for s in stmts {\n        match s {\n          ast.ComptimeFor { .. } => (),\n          ast.Let { pat, value, .. } => {\n            termination.struct_expr(mut st, value, v)\n            w := termination.piece(value, v)\n           