es(\n        kernel.depends_on(pq),\n        kernel.depends_on(p),\n      )!, kernel.Step { rule: \"eq_mp\", premises: [pq, p] }))\n    } else {\n      Err(\"eq_mp: the theorem isn't the equation's left side\")\n    },\n    None => Err(\"eq_mp: not an equation\"),\n  }\n}","old_text":"/// `A ⊢ p = q` and `B ⊢ p` give `A ∪ B ⊢ q`.\npub fn replace_by_equal(\n  pq: kernel.Theorem,\n  p: kernel.Theorem,\n) -> Result[kernel.Theorem, String] {\n  match kernel.split_equation(kernel.conclusion(pq)) {\n    Some((l, r)) => if kernel.same_term(l, kernel.conclusion(p)) {\n      Ok(kernel.make_theorem(kernel.union_of_terms(\n        kernel.assumptions(pq),\n        kernel.assumptions(p),\n      ), r, kernel.joined_dependencies(\n        kernel.depends_on(pq),\n        kernel.depends_on(p),\n      )!))\n    } else {\n      Err(\"eq_mp: the theorem isn't the equation's left side\")\n    },\n    None => Err(\"eq_mp: not an equation\"),\n  }\n}"},{"name":"kernel.equal_if_each_implies_other","kind":"fn","old":"c269aedb2aff744d","new":"ca0de1b07cf8d9d1","interface_changed":false,"affected":["kernel_logic.equal_to_true","kernel_logic.equal_to_false","kernel_logic.equal_by_both_directions","kernel_tactics.constructor","kernel_logic.logic_rewrites","kernel_logic.rewrites_of_body","kernel_translate.flipped_distinct","kernel_tactics.apply_tactic","kernel_cli.check_script","kernel_tactics.logic_not_not","kernel_translate.for_each_value","kernel_logic.rewrites_fixing","kernel_translate.add_datatypes","kernel_tactics.run","kernel_cli.check_source","kernel_cli.check_module","kernel_tactics.split_on_condition","kernel_tactics.split_on_named","kernel_translate.case_same","kernel_translate.record_eta","kernel_logic.rewrites_of","kernel_tactics.rules_from","kernel_tactics.simp_with","kernel_tactics.assumption_facts","kernel_tactics.facts_rules","kernel_translate.add_datatype","kernel_translate.add_decls","kernel_tactics.close_with","kernel_cli.base_theory","kernel_cli.command","kernel_tactics.spli